<title>FRANCE: Remy shares plunge on year results.</title>
<headline>Remy shares plunge on year results.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in drinks group Remy-Cointreau fell sharply on Wednesday after the company reported a drop in its full year profits to March 31.</p>
<p>The company said its net profit dropped to 36 million francs from 120 million. Its first quarter sales were up by 13 percent, it added.</p>
<p>Remy added it expected to benefit only partly from the dollar's rise.</p>
<p>At 0824 GMT, Remy was down 7.99 percent at 137 francs.</p>
